<!--
    Wazuh rules for UniFi CEF syslog messages
    Requires the "ubiquiti" decoder from https://github.com/evangress/wazuh-unifi-decoder
    UniFi docs (CEF keys, event taxonomy):
    https://help.ui.com/hc/en-us/articles/33349041044119-UniFi-System-Logs-SIEM-Integration

    Notes:
    - All rules hang off 100010, which matches anything decoded by the "ubiquiti" decoder.
    - Wazuh tries sibling rules from highest level to lowest, not in file order. A rule that
      should lower the level of a broader match must be its child (see 100103 under 100104).
      A high CEF severity (100390/100391) therefore wins over a lower-level specific rule.
    - UniFi CEF severity (event.severity) is mapped to Wazuh levels:
      0-3 -> 2 (archived, not alerted), 4-6 -> 5, 7-8 -> 10, 9-10 -> 12
    - Rule ID range reserved in this file: 100010-100399

